-- Applied Physics | ESE | easy | 4900971911010125 | theory | reused from Applied Physics (4400971921010125)
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4900971911010125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Definition of unit in the context of Units, Dimensions and Measurements. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Inertia in the context of Laws of Motion. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Stress & strain along with their types in the context of Properties of Matter. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Current electricity: current in the context of Electro-Magnetism. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Definition of unit is covered in “Units, Dimensions and Measurements”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Fundamental and Derived units, systems of units- CGS, MKS and SI, introduction to accuracy, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Fundamental and Derived units; systems of units- CGS; MKS and SI; introduction to accuracy. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Newton''s first law says an object remains at rest or moves uniformly in a straight line unless a non-zero resultant force acts. Inertia is resistance to changing motion.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Newton''s first law of motion; momentum; Newton’s second law of motion; conservation of momentum. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Stress & strain along with their types is covered in “Properties of Matter”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Hooke''s law and modulus of elasticity-Young, bulk and modulus of rigidity, Viscosity, newton''s law of viscosity, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Hooke''s law and modulus of elasticity-Young; bulk and modulus of rigidity; Viscosity; newton''s law of viscosity. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Current electricity: current is covered in “Electro-Magnetism”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to EMF and Ohm''s law, resistance, series and parallel, Magnetism: Magnetic field and properties, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as EMF and Ohm''s law; resistance; series and parallel; Magnetism: Magnetic field and properties. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

