VALUES (4900971911010126, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Definition of unit in the context of Units, Dimensions and Measurements. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Inertia in the context of Laws of Motion. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Light: Properties in the context of Waves: Light & Sound. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Fundamental and Derived units in the context of Units, Dimensions and Measurements. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Definition of unit is covered in “Units, Dimensions and Measurements”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Fundamental and Derived units, systems of units- CGS, MKS and SI, introduction to accuracy, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Fundamental and Derived units; systems of units- CGS; MKS and SI; introduction to accuracy. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Newton''s first law says an object remains at rest or moves uniformly in a straight line unless a non-zero resultant force acts. Inertia is resistance to changing motion.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Newton''s first law of motion; momentum; Newton’s second law of motion; conservation of momentum. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Light: Properties is covered in “Waves: Light & Sound”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Reflection, Refraction, Snell’s law, Dispersion of light, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Reflection; Refraction; Snell’s law; Dispersion of light. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** A unit is a standard for expressing a physical quantity. Fundamental units are independent standards; derived units combine them. Convert values to compatible units before calculations.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Definition of unit; systems of units- CGS; MKS and SI; introduction to accuracy. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Applied Physics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

