VALUES (490093200103011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applicat in the context of Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain  PNP and NPN transistors in the context of Transistor characteristics and biasing 10. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain half wave in the context of Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C in the context of Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applicat appears in “Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters., provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters., Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  PNP and NPN transistors appears in “Transistor characteristics and biasing 10”. Define its role and features, relate it to conduction through transistor leakage current, relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to conduction through transistor leakage current, relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** half wave appears in “Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters., Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters., Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C appears in “Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, π filters., Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, π filters., Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

