VALUES (4900932001030112, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving π filters. in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5 in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving conduction through transistor leakage current in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** π filters. appears in “Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5 appears in “Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters., provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters.. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** conduction through transistor leakage current appears in “Transistor characteristics and biasing 10”. Define its role and features, relate it to  PNP and NPN transistors, relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  PNP and NPN transistors, relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB appears in “Transistor characteristics and biasing 10”. Define its role and features, relate it to  PNP and NPN transistors, conduction through transistor leakage current, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  PNP and NPN transistors, conduction through transistor leakage current, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

