VALUES (4900932001030134, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving  Common emitter amplifier.  Common collector amplifier  Multistage amplifier in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving  JFET and MOSFET  Special purpose diode in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving  Working principle of oscillator  Different types of oscillators: Hartley oscillator in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving  Cables: coaxial cable in Basics of Electronics Engineering. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  Common emitter amplifier.  Common collector amplifier  Multistage amplifier appears in “Transistor as an amplifier: 2.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to Transistor as an amplifier: 2.5, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Transistor as an amplifier: 2.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  JFET and MOSFET  Special purpose diode appears in “Special purpose diode and Applications 5”. Define its role and features, relate it to Zener diode & it''s application,  Photo diode  LDR  Photovoltaic Cell  Light Emitting Diode  Varactor Diode  Digital Display, Special purpose diode and Applications 5, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Zener diode & it''s application,  Photo diode  LDR  Photovoltaic Cell  Light Emitting Diode  Varactor Diode  Digital Display, Special purpose diode and Applications 5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  Working principle of oscillator  Different types of oscillators: Hartley oscillator appears in “Oscillators 4”. Define its role and features, relate it to Colpitts oscillator, Phase- Shift Oscillator, Wien Bridge Oscillator, Crystal Oscillator, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Colpitts oscillator, Phase- Shift Oscillator, Wien Bridge Oscillator, Crystal Oscillator, FET Oscillator.. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  Cables: coaxial cable appears in “Cables and Connectors 1.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to twisted pair cable and fiber optic cable  Connectors: coaxial cable connectors, RJ-45, RS-232, HDMI connectors. Total 28.5 100 Syllabus for Diploma Engineering Information and Communication Technology, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to twisted pair cable and fiber optic cable  Connectors: coaxial cable connectors, RJ-45, RS-232, HDMI connectors. Total 28.5 100 Syllabus for Diploma Engineering Information and Communication Technology, Cables and Connectors 1.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

